  "slug": "dark-4pcf-cb95",
  "summary": "New forecasts for Simons Observatory, CMB-S4, LSST and Euclid-like surveys test whether w0wa hints and new-physics claims survive priors and systematics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is forecasting and method development for testing departures from LCDM with upcoming data. On dark energy, a Bayesian MCMC forecast asks whether Simons Observatory and CMB-S4 can separate w0waCDM from LCDM shadow models. A separate analysis finds that the CMB+BAO preference for early recombination disappears under w0wa, which yields the lowest AIC. Lensing ratios of galaxy-CMB and galaxy-galaxy lensing are proposed as geometric probes of dark energy and curvature for LSST and Simons Observatory. Several papers address systematics and tractability. Neglected light-cone and relativistic effects bias local fNL by ~2σ for a Euclid-like survey and by >10σ for a MegaMapper-like one. A Woodbury factorization makes unbinned LSST-scale supernova fits feasible, cutting fit time from ~10 weeks to ~1.5 hr. Other methodological contributions include a hybrid EFT for diffuse-baryon power spectra and binaryfog, a surrogate for testing how astrophysical priors affect new-physics evidence in pulsar timing arrays.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
